  "id": "197de793-9331-59c1-b4ea-65d7d7ef0c71",
  "slug": "salted-grapefruit-fizz-recipe-8717911",
  "name": "Salted Grapefruit Fizz",
  "recipe_type": "drink",
  "brief_description": "A salted grapefruit fizz is a yummy non-alcoholic punch that will surely please your guests at your next party. Add a retro vibe with a citrus ice ring.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "To make the salted grapefruit cordial: Remove strips of zest from 1 ruby grapefruit with a vegetable peeler, avoiding any white pith. Stir grapefruit zest and sugar together in a jar. Chill, covered, for 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Squeeze juice from the grapefruit and measure out 1/2 cup juice. Pour 1/2 cup grapefruit juice, fresh lime juice, and water over the sugar mixture in the jar. Stir in kosher salt. Stir or shake mixture to dissolve sugar. Strain out zest; chill for 1 hour or cover and keep chilled for up to 3 days."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "To make the punch: Combine salted grapefruit cordial, grapefruit juice, and lime juice in a punch bowl. Chill until ready to serve; pour in club soda before serving with citrus ice ring, if using."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "To make a citrus ice ring: Fill an ice ring mold with very thin half slices of grapefruit and very thin slices of lime. Fill ring halfway with water; freeze until firm, about 30 minutes. Add more water to fill mold, freeze until firm, about 2 hours."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
